  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Robert D. Webb Jr. is an American businessman and chairman and chief executive of Louisiana Cat, a Caterpillar equipment dealer. Previously its president, he is a documented part-owner of the business. His career centres on machinery sales, rental and support for customers in construction, industry and the energy sector across Louisiana.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 90,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Primary ownership and leadership records establish the individual; trade reporting establishes operating scope."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S3",
      "S5",
      "S6"
    ],
    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Robert D. Webb Jr. is an American businessman and chairman and chief executive of Louisiana Cat, a Caterpillar equipment dealer. Previously its president, he is a documented part-owner of the business. His career centres on machinery sales, rental and support for customers in construction, industry and the energy sector across Louisiana.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "When Robert Webb decided to build a dedicated rental division, he recruited an experienced rental operator to lead it. Donald Charbonnet knew both the local market and the demands of offshore and industrial customers. The task was to organise rentals separately from the dealership, and the resulting Louisiana Rents network expanded across the state.\n\nWebb also signed the agreement that made Louisiana Cat the first dealer in the Americas to qualify for Caterpillar's Gold-level propulsion programme. Staff completed technical training to support customers purchasing an entire propulsion system. The additional equipment carried power from the engine through the shaft to the propeller.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 87,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Full contemporary accounts support his recruitment decision and personal signing role without assigning staff quotations or engineering inventions to him."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S6",
      "S7"
    ],
    "word_count": 102,
    "html": "<p>When Robert Webb decided to build a dedicated rental division, he recruited an experienced rental operator to lead it. Donald Charbonnet knew both the local market and the demands of offshore and industrial customers. The task was to organise rentals separately from the dealership, and the resulting Louisiana Rents network expanded across the state.</p>\r\n<p>Webb also signed the agreement that made Louisiana Cat the first dealer in the Americas to qualify for Caterpillar's Gold-level propulsion programme. Staff completed technical training to support customers purchasing an entire propulsion system. The additional equipment carried power from the engine through the shaft to the propeller.</p>\r\n"
  },
